# PROJECT CLOSURE AND HANDOVER 

## Purpose

The purpose of this Project Closure and Handover Plan is to define the activities required to formally complete the Emergency Department Patient Flow Transformation project.

Project closure ensures that all deliverables have been completed, stakeholders have accepted the outcomes, operational teams are prepared to take ownership, and lessons are captured for future improvement.



# Project Closure Approach

The project will be formally closed when:

- All agreed deliverables are completed.
- Project objectives have been assessed.
- Solution ownership has transferred to operational teams.
- Documentation has been completed.
- Outstanding issues have been transferred.
- Lessons learned have been captured.



# Closure Activities

The project closure process consists of the following activities:

1. Deliverable Review
2. Stakeholder Acceptance
3. Operational Handover
4. Documentation Completion
5. Benefits Transition
6. Lessons Learned Review
7. Final Project Closure Approval



# Deliverable Review

The Project Manager will review all project deliverables to confirm completion.

Completed deliverables include:

## Project Documentation

- Project Charter
- Business Case
- Project Plan
- Risk Management Plan
- Stakeholder Management Plan
- Governance Documentation



## Solution Documentation

- System Design Documentation
- Testing Documentation
- User Guides
- Technical Documentation
- Support Procedures



## Change Management Documentation

- Training Materials
- Communication Records
- Adoption Reports



# Stakeholder Acceptance

Before closure, key stakeholders will confirm that project outcomes meet expectations.

Acceptance activities include:

- Reviewing project objectives
- Confirming deliverables
- Reviewing outstanding issues
- Approving transition into operational support

Stakeholder approval will be obtained from:

- Executive Sponsor
- Clinical Lead
- IT Lead
- Information Governance Team
- Operational Managers



# Operational Handover

After project completion, responsibility will transition from the project team to operational teams.

The handover process ensures that the organisation can continue managing the solution effectively.



# Handover Package

The operational handover will include:

## Technical Documentation

Includes:

- System configuration information
- Integration details
- Technical support procedures



## User Documentation

Includes:

- User guides
- Training materials
- Frequently asked questions



## Governance Documentation

Includes:

- Ownership responsibilities
- Escalation routes
- Support arrangements



## Performance Documentation

Includes:

- Initial performance results
- KPI measurements
- Benefits tracking approach



# Support Transition Model

The solution will move into business-as-usual operations through a structured support model.



## Operational Support Team

Responsible for:

- Daily system management
- User support
- Monitoring performance



## IT Support Team

Responsible for:

- Technical incidents
- System maintenance
- Security monitoring



## Supplier Support

Responsible for:

- Product issues
- Software updates
- Technical assistance



# Outstanding Issues Management

Any unresolved issues at project closure will be transferred into operational management.

Each issue will include:

- Description
- Owner
- Priority
- Target resolution date
- Escalation process



# Lessons Learned

Lessons learned will be captured to improve future healthcare transformation projects.



# What Went Well

Examples:

- Strong stakeholder involvement
- Early clinical engagement
- Structured governance approach
- Phased implementation strategy



# Challenges Identified

Examples:

- Managing staff availability
- Balancing operational pressures
- Integrating existing systems
- Supporting user adoption



# Recommendations for Future Projects

Future projects should:

- Engage users from the beginning
- Include cybersecurity and information governance early
- Maintain clear communication
- Use phased implementation approaches
- Continue measuring benefits after delivery



# Final Project Review

The final project review will assess:

## Scope Performance

Was the project delivered according to agreed objectives?



## Timeline Performance

Was the project completed according to the planned schedule?



## Financial Performance

Was the project delivered within the approved budget?



## Quality Performance

Did the solution meet required standards?



## Benefits Performance

Did the project achieve expected improvements?



# Project Closure Approval

The project will be officially closed after approval from the Project Board.

Closure approval confirms:

- Deliverables completed
- Handover completed
- Documentation completed
- Lessons captured
- Operational ownership transferred



